findings.body:
The assertion requires **both** CSP message formats to match the same log entry:

::diff{file="src/Components/test/E2ETest/ServerExecutionTests/WebSocketCompressionTests.cs" lines="107-111"}

The two patterns are disjoint: the old one requires `security - Refused to frame '...' because an ancestor violates ...` while the new one requires `security - Framing '...' violates ...`. A single `logs[0].Message` can never contain both, so `EmbeddingServerAppInsideIframe_WithCompressionEnabled_Fails` fails on every browser. The failure message itself says "match one of the CSP error patterns", which confirms `||` was intended. The upstream fix that introduced these regexes (commit `3132e7b1`, PR #64326) used `||`; this PR changed it to `&&`.

::callout{type="warning"}
This is a deterministic test failure, not a flake. It will block the Components E2E leg and removes coverage of the CSP behavior when the assertion is adjusted ad hoc.

::suggestion{file="src/Components/test/E2ETest/ServerExecutionTests/WebSocketCompressionTests.cs" lines="107-110"}
Assert.True(
    ParseErrorMessageRegexOld.IsMatch(logs[0].Message) ||
    ParseErrorMessageRegexNew.IsMatch(logs[0].Message),
    $"Expected log message to match one of the CSP error patterns: {ParseErrorMessageRegexOld} or {ParseErrorMessageRegexNew}. Actual: {logs[0].Message}");

`ReceiveAsync` now consumes and discards the frame returned by a 0-byte poll:

::diff{file="src/SignalR/server/StackExchangeRedis/test/RedisEndToEnd.cs" lines="406-417"}

The SignalR client's receive loop deliberately performs a 0-byte read and then a buffered read for the **same** frame:

::code{file="src/SignalR/clients/csharp/Http.Connections.Client/src/Internal/WebSocketsTransport.cs" lines="441-461"}

With the reset moved above the zero-byte `return`, the completed `_receiveTcs` is replaced before the buffered read runs. That buffered read therefore awaits a brand-new result instead of the frame the poll just observed, and `res.Item2` from the polled frame is never copied. In `StatefulReconnectPreservesMessageFromOtherServer`, the preserved "test message" arrives as that frame, so the buffered read blocks until `DefaultTimeout()` fails.

::callout{type="info"}
The only consumer is `StatefulReconnectPreservesMessageFromOtherServer`, currently quarantined for issue #62435, so this is not gating CI today. The helper's contract is still broken and the test will hang as soon as it is un-quarantined.

::suggestion{file="src/SignalR/server/StackExchangeRedis/test/RedisEndToEnd.cs" lines="408-416"}
var res = await _receiveTcs.Task;
// Handle zero-byte reads
if (buffer.Count == 0)
{
    return res.Item1;
}
_receiveTcs = new(TaskCreationOptions.RunContinuationsAsynchronously);
res.Item2.CopyTo(buffer);
return res.Item1;
